 to be Speaker by other Members of Parliament. During debates they keep order and call MPs to speak.\nL158: \nL159: 【58†Image: There is no description available for this image (ID: 204910)】\nL160: \nL161: 【58†Image: Reflection of image】\nL162: ### Rt Hon Sir Lindsay Hoyle MP\nL163: \nL164: The Rt Hon Sir Lindsay Hoyle, Member of Parliament for the constituency of Chorley, Lancashire, is a three time elected Speaker and has held the office of Speaker of the House of Commons since 4 November 2019.\nL165: \nL166: ## 【59†Biography of the Speaker Sir Lindsay Hoyle】\nL167: \nL168: 【60†Image: There is no description available for this image (ID: 202546)】\nL169: \nL170: Learn more about the Speaker, Sir Lindsay Hoyle\nL171: ## 【61†Speaker and the Chamber】\nL172: \nL173: 【62†Image: There is no description available for this image (ID: 153499)】\nL174: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Lord Speaker - UK Parliament (https://www.parliament.uk/business/lords/lord-speaker/)\nciteturn28view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn27view0\",\"id\":61}); Total lines: 266\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLeader of the House of Lords - UK Parliament (https://www.parliament.uk/business/lords/whos-in-the-house-of-lords/members-and-their-roles/leader-of-the-house-of-lords/)\nciteturn28view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn27view0\",\"id\":62}); Total lines: 224\n"
